    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d708-a1">

                <pb facs="0788" n="708" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg708"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Buck to Baron Komura.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-03-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 22,
                    1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur le Ministre</hi>: In compliance with
                    telegraphic instructions from my Government, I have the honor to inform your
                    excellency that His Imperial Majesty’s Government having given the assurance
                    that citizens of the United States in Japan will receive equality of treatment
                    with the nationals of other states in the matter of house tax, the United States
                    Government would like to agree, by an exchange of notes with the Imperial
                    Government, that the two Governments will abide by the decision of the principle
                    involved which may be settled by arbitration between Japan and the other states,
                    touching both the house and income tax, and that the Imperial Government will
                    apply the principle of equality to nationals of the United States, France,
                    Germany, and Great Britain.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. E. Buck.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
